menu "Sendspin player"

    config SENDSPIN_PLAYER_ENABLE
        bool "Sendspin player (Music Assistant)"
        # its buffers live in PSRAM; the WM8804 I2C driver's clock hook and
        # slave mode are not wired into the Sendspin output yet
        depends on SPIRAM && !SPDIF_WM8804
        default n
        help
            Play Sendspin streams (Music Assistant's synchronized audio
            protocol) next to snapcast. While a Sendspin stream plays it owns
            the audio output; snapcast plays again 2 s after it ends.
            Needs PSRAM and ESP-IDF 5.5.2 or later. Not available with the
            WM8804 I2C driver (SPDIF_WM8804) yet.

    config SENDSPIN_PLAYER_PORT
        int "Sendspin WebSocket port"
        depends on SENDSPIN_PLAYER_ENABLE
        range 1 65535
        default 8928
        help
            The server (Music Assistant) connects to this port. 8928 is the
            port the Sendspin spec recommends.

    config SENDSPIN_UNPAIRED_ACCESS
        bool "Let servers play without pairing"
        depends on SENDSPIN_PLAYER_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            With this on, any Sendspin server on the network may play on this
            device without pairing first; Music Assistant then adds it with
            no setup step (the same default ESPHome uses). Turn it off to
            accept only paired servers ("require pairing").

            The Status tab of the settings page can change this at run time
            (kept across restarts); this sets the starting value.

            A server pairs with the 8-digit code shown on the Status tab,
            while the pairing window is open: a short press of the device
            button or "Allow pairing" on the Status tab opens it for 5
            minutes. Pair Music Assistant first, then require pairing:
            Music Assistant does not reconnect by itself after an unpaired
            connection is refused.

endmenu
